
Ex.No:5 Queries Using ANY, ALL, IN, EXISTS, NOT EXISTS, UNION, INTERSECT and Constraints

Aim:
To write and execute SQL queries using the ANY, ALL, IN, EXISTS, and NOT EXISTS operators, the set operations UNION and INTERSECT, and to reinforce the use of integrity constraints (PRIMARY KEY, FOREIGN KEY, UNIQUE, NOT NULL, CHECK, DEFAULT) on a related set of tables.

Theory:
Operator / Clause	Purpose
IN	Checks whether a value matches any value in a list or subquery result
ANY / SOME	Compares a value to each value returned by a subquery; true if the comparison holds for at least one row
ALL	Compares a value to each value returned by a subquery; true only if the comparison holds for every row
EXISTS	Returns true if the subquery returns at least one row
NOT EXISTS	Returns true if the subquery returns no rows
UNION	Combines results of two queries, removing duplicate rows
UNION ALL	Combines results of two queries, keeping duplicate rows
INTERSECT	Returns only rows common to both queries
EXCEPT / MINUS	Returns rows from the first query that do not appear in the second

Note: UNION, UNION ALL, INTERSECT, and EXCEPT require every participating SELECT to return the same number of columns with compatible data types.
Database Schema Used
This lab extends the CollegeDB schema with Course and Enrollment tables so that meaningful subqueries and set operations can be written across related data.

 Reuse / extend the CollegeDB schema from the constraints lab
CREATE DATABASE IF NOT EXISTS CollegeDB;
USE CollegeDB;

CREATE TABLE Department ( dept_id     INT PRIMARY KEY, dept_name   VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL UNIQUE);

CREATE TABLE Student ( roll_no     INT PRIMARY KEY,
    name        VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,
    age         INT CHECK (age >= 17 AND age <= 30),
    email       VARCHAR(50) UNIQUE,
    gender      VARCHAR(10) DEFAULT 'Not Specified',
    dept_id     INT,
    FOREIGN KEY (dept_id) REFERENCES Department(dept_id)
);


CREATE TABLE Course ( course_id   INT PRIMARY KEY,
    course_name VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,
    credits     INT CHECK (credits BETWEEN 1 AND 6),
    dept_id     INT,
    FOREIGN KEY (dept_id) REFERENCES Department(dept_id)
);

CREATE TABLE Enrollment ( roll_no     INT, course_id   INT,
    marks       INT CHECK (marks BETWEEN 0 AND 100),
    PRIMARY KEY (roll_no, course_id),
    FOREIGN KEY (roll_no) REFERENCES Student(roll_no),
    FOREIGN KEY (course_id) REFERENCES Course(course_id)
);

